Z||000001||beer_stud_21||08-02-2001||04:29 AM||||Hey,<P>I'm about to move to Bend, OR.  In a month or so.  There are very few PFF members in Oregon (and very few on the west coast for that matter.)  I think I read somewhere about a Oregon fiero club.  I will have to look for the info for you/us.  By the way, have you seen very many Fieros for sale in Oregon.  I've only found one online.  In Eugene I believe. a 55k mile 87GT I believe.  Nice condition, but he wants something like 6k for it.  <P>-Marlin||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||08-02-2001||09:50 AM||||I was in Oregon in late June, and only saw like 4-5 Fieros all week. Saw a "flawless" blue 87 coupe in Grant's Pass and a suhweet silver 87 or 88 coupe in Astoria. <BR>Bunch of great twisty roads, though. Too bad I was in a rent-a-sled.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fatal Error||08-02-2001||06:25 PM||||The whole reason why I got interested in fieros was an 85gt that was for sale just down the street from me. 1995.00 it didn't last long, unfort I couldn't get the fundage to buy her. How ever there is an 87 coupe in my complex that has a bad rod cap bearing with 65kmiles on it got the VIN today (1G2PE11R2HP236045) with t-tops. I haven't settled on a price but im sure I can get it for cheap cause the guy doesn't have the time to do the rebuild. The interior is trashed unfort. ...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> Other then that if you do a search on auto trader and limit the search to 200 miles and out of the 97007 (my area code) you will see there are a few for sale.<P>As far as the club, that would be sweet. I would love to meet some fellow fiero peeps. <P>Marlin, sure we can hook up if ya ever make it to the Portland area.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>There are a lot of nice twisty turny roads through mountain passes to the coast ... they are hella fun, a lot of 35mph corners.<P>Thanks for the info guys!||||reg||10
Z||000004||beer_stud_21||08-02-2001||06:30 PM||||I've been thinkin about how nice it would be to have a 87 couple with T-tops.  I like that body style, and T-tops would be awsome.  But since I've finally got my 85GT to start up im starting to wonder.  The V6 sounds so awsome.  I think driving around and hearing that nice rumble would be half the fun.  Instead fo rebuilding that I4 you should swap a 4.9 caddy or Quad4.  Thats what I want to do someday.  Portland is a ways from bend, but if I have a good reason and a fun car I dont see why that drive would be outa the question!  hehe.<P>-Marlin||||reg||1
